From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:53:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: read back the OTG and DIG stereo state

DC programs frame-sequential stereo in three places: the OTG alternates
the eyes (OTG_STEREO_CONTROL, with the current eye in OTG_STEREO_STATUS;
optc1_enable_stereo()), the DIG front end takes the OTG's stereo sync
and drives MSA MISC1 bits 2:1 on DisplayPort (DIG_FE_CNTL
DIG_STEREOSYNC_SELECT and DIG_STEREOSYNC_GATE_EN;
enc1_setup_stereo_sync()), and the VSC SDP that names the stereo method
is sent as generic packet 0 (DP_SEC_CNTL DP_SEC_GSP0_ENABLE;
enc1_stream_encoder_update_dp_info_packets()).
None of these registers is read back anywhere, and the DTN log prints
none of them, so nothing shows what the hardware was told.

- struct dcn_otg_state gains OTG_STEREO_CONTROL, OTG_STEREO_STATUS and
  OTG_3D_STRUCTURE_CONTROL, read by optc1_read_otg_state() and
  optc31_read_otg_state(), the read_otg_state hook of every DCN OTG.
  Their existing users (the DTN log, optc1_get_hw_timing()) ignore them.
- A new stream encoder hook, read_stereo_state, implemented once as
  enc1_read_stereo_state() for every DIO stream encoder (DCN 1.0 to 6.0
  use struct dcn10_stream_encoder): the DIG stereo sync fields,
  DP_SEC_CNTL with its stream and GSP0 enables, DP_MSA_MISC and, on
  DCN 1.x and 2.x whose generic packets sit behind the AFMT_GENERIC
  registers, the header and data of GSP0, read through the window
  enc1_update_generic_info_packet() writes them through. DCN 3.0 and
  later keep generic packets in the VPG; GSP0 is not read there
  (gsp0_read is false). The virtual and HPO encoders have no hook.

amdgpu_dm's stereo debugfs file is the first user. Reading GSP0 selects
generic packet 0 in AFMT_VBI_PACKET_CONTROL, as every write of a generic
packet does first, so callers hold the same lock as DC's programming.

Assisted-by: LLM
